#: ../../source/cheerio_Readme.md:171
msgid "Selectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cheerio_Readme.md:173
msgid ""
"Cheerio's selector implementation is nearly identical to jQuery's, so the"
" API is very similar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cheerio_Readme.md:175
msgid "\\$( selector, [context], [root] )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cheerio_Readme.md:177
msgid ""
"`selector` searches within the `context` scope which searches within the "
"`root` scope. `selector` and `context` can be a string expression, DOM "
"Element, array of DOM elements, or cheerio object. `root` is typically "
"the HTML document string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cheerio_Readme.md:179
msgid ""
"This selector method is the starting point for traversing and "
"manipulating the document. Like jQuery, it's the primary method for "
"selecting elements in the document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cheerio_Readme.md:192
msgid "XML Namespaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cheerio_Readme.md:194
msgid ""
"You can select with XML Namespaces but [due to the CSS "
"specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-css3-selectors-20110929"
"/#attribute-selectors), the colon (`:`) needs to be escaped for the "
"selector to be valid."
msgstr ""

